"text": "- **Not run: mutation.** No `run --mutants` (`inputs#I1` item 4). Each guard's strength is its one-shot control   (below); a control mutates source, so it is no entry. - **Not run: live legs.** No live `claude` start (`inputs#I1` item 2): every mapped value is the CLI's own declared   value, read from source; the reading that the real CLI fires StopFailure with them is «The 2.1.325 recorded   fixture set»'s. Live starts asked: 0. - **No smoke.** No boot-path touchpoint: `src/cmd/run.rs` changes only in its test table; the start path, the plugin   files and the snapshot are untouched; the booted cases boot their wrapper themselves. - **Why CI is read.** The operator pass pushes the chunk's tree and reads its run on CI's one leg, `ubuntu-latest`   (the diag schema conformance gate G4 reads the new word there). No OS-conditional site is added. - **Thresholds.** The chunk adds no numeric threshold. The booted case's waits are WITHIN = 12 s, below the mutants   profile's 15 s kill and cargo-mutants' 20 s floor `(test-plan · bootstrap-phases-derive-for-route-setup-project/decision/mutants-kill-below-cargo-mutants-timeout)`;   each control's `--timeout` sits above its filtered entry's own run time and below nothing a mutant reaches. - **Controls, each one-shot through `gate.py control`** (gate-contract §Control), each on an entry filtered to the   guard's own cases, its case by name:   - `cause-map` — `--timeout 300` on entry 5; guard: the `rate_limit` arm of `api_error_cause` (the word then reads     `api-error`); case the map table's `rate_limit` row.   - `cause-check` — `--timeout 300` on entry 8; guard: `TurnEndCause::from_name` in `hook_event_line`'s `cause_ok`     (any string admitted); case the appended-line table's error-text row.   - `unknown-line` — `--timeout 300` on entry 7; guard: the `unknown-value` call after `normalise` in     `src/cmd/hook.rs`; case `handle_logs_an_unknown_error_value_by_its_code_only`.   - `cause-crossing` — `--timeout 600` on entry 10; guard: the classified word in `data_of`'s StopFailure arm (the     literal `api-error` written again); case `hook_stop_failure_names_the_cause_of_each_cli_error_word`.   The exact `old`/`new` texts are written by /implement against its own diff; «holds» = the named case ran and   FAILED with no TIMEOUT line (`inputs#I1` item 4). Control ids stay within 16 characters."
}
